  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 1237 PM CST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nThanksgiving and Black Friday are expected to have mostly fall-like \nconditions with highs ion the 50s on Thanksgiving and 60s on Friday. \nThe warming trend continues through Saturday where highs move up \ninto the upper 60s to low 70s. A cold front moves through the area \nlate Saturday and early Sunday. This frontal passage will be dry and \nusher in colder air knocking highs for Sunday down about 10-15 \ndegrees compared to Saturday. Above average temperatures come right \nback for Monday and Tuesday next week as ridging moves in across the \nPlains. The forecast remains dry through the extended with \nprecipitation chances holding near 0%. \n\n-Stickney",
